  "fibres": [],
  "measures": [],
  "notes": "A collimated Gaussian beam (w 1 mm, 633 nm) through a fused silica axicon with a 1° base angle. The cone bends every part of the beam by the same angle, 0.46°, towards the axis, so the beam crosses itself along a line rather than at a point: a Bessel beam. Its central lobe is J0² of kθr, about 28 µm across at half height, and it keeps it for roughly w/θ = 125 mm. Beyond that the light carries on as a cone and opens into a ring. The first screen samples the Bessel zone without blocking it (look at its Diffraction tab: a bright core and rings 40 µm apart); the second, at 300 mm, shows the ring."
